<ZonePage lang="en" title="Living in David, Chiriquí" description="Guide to living in David, Panama's western capital: services, climate, cost of living, and gateway to Boquete and Volcán." emoji="🌆" zone="ciudad" locationName="David" climate="Hot & sunny, 28–34°C" rentRange="From $500 / month" profile="Families, budget-focused, gateway city" internet="Good (fiber available)" heroImage="/img/areas/panama-city-waterfront.webp"
  intro="David is the regional capital of Chiriquí and Panama's second or third largest city, depending on how you count. It's hot, practical, and seriously affordable — and it serves as the gateway to Boquete, Volcán, and the beaches of the Pacific coast. Many expats use it as a base rather than a permanent home, though a growing number settle here for the combination of full urban services and very low costs."
