  faqs={[
    {q:"Why do expats choose David over Boquete?", a:"Cost. A furnished 2-bedroom house in David rents for $500–$700/month compared to $800–$1,500+ in Boquete. For expats who want full urban services — hospitals, PriceSmart, malls — at a fraction of the cost, David delivers. The trade-off is the heat and the absence of the cooler highland climate."},
    {q:"Is David safe for expats?", a:"David is generally considered safe by Panamanian standards. Normal urban precautions apply — avoid displaying valuables, be aware of your surroundings at night in downtown areas. Most expats in David live comfortable, incident-free lives."},
    {q:"What healthcare is available in David?", a:"David has two private hospitals: Hospital Chiriquí and Hospital Mae Lewis. Hospital Chiriquí is the regional reference hospital for western Panama, with 24/7 emergency services and a range of specialties. Serious or highly specialized cases are typically referred to Panama City."},
    {q:"Is David a good base for exploring western Panama?", a:"Yes — it's ideal. Boquete is 30 minutes away, Volcán is 45 minutes, the Pacific coast beaches are 60–90 minutes, and domestic flights to Panama City take about 45 minutes. Many expats use David as a practical hub while exploring the region before settling in a specific town."},
